From 22e565e0867a1a68c7ebed1a565922baa57f8bfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashish Kumar Singh <ashishkmr472@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:50:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [XLA:CPU] YNNPACK's unary kernels read an input of any
 innermost stride as given

YNN's unary kernels read their input contiguously in its innermost dimension, and make_unary_elementwise_impl
asserted it, an assert compiled out of a release: a bf16 convert of a broadcast scalar, a stride-zero alias,
read past the scalar as contiguous memory (NaN or garbage by process). The implementation gathers a block of
an input whose innermost dimension is not contiguous into a buffer of the call's own, never writing the input,
which its producer and other consumers share. Tested: a shared broadcast converted twice, reductions beside a
shared clamp broadcast, and row sums of squares and softmax rows.
